  AloneLines:
  - "Sand in the bread, sand in the bed. At least it's my sand."
  - "Hot by day, cold by night, and not a soul to argue with about which is worse."
  - "Shovel it out, {name}. The dunes will walk right in if you let them."
  - "Haven't seen a face in a month. Saw a lizard. It blinked first."
  - "The quiet out here is big. You learn to fill it with your own voice."
